WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.940
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs

01:35.040 --> 01:39.950
Episode 3:
Vitalis Troupe

01:54.610 --> 02:01.760
Mother, was I really a foundling?
Am I not your child?

02:02.440 --> 02:07.220
I never stopped thinking...
that you were my daughter.

02:08.390 --> 02:09.570
Mother...

02:14.650 --> 02:18.740
Mother! Mother!

02:18.920 --> 02:23.290
I'm here, mother!

02:30.210 --> 02:31.660
Mother...

02:32.240 --> 02:33.460
I...

02:35.060 --> 02:38.140
I... Mother...

02:39.750 --> 02:41.310
I can't make you sad.

02:45.280 --> 02:46.070
Goodbye.

02:49.080 --> 02:52.870
Goodbye. Goodbye!

02:53.510 --> 02:56.610
Mother!

03:15.220 --> 03:16.750
Joli-Coeur!

03:17.360 --> 03:18.850
Wait!

03:21.370 --> 03:22.880
Joli-Coeur!

03:23.530 --> 03:25.050
Now you can't escape!

03:32.830 --> 03:37.300
Good morning. Is it time for breakfast?

03:39.400 --> 03:44.670
If you want bread, then you have to work.
That's a rule of the Vitalis troupe.

03:46.050 --> 03:52.170
We got wood for the fire and drinking water.
But what's crybaby Remy been doing?

03:53.060 --> 03:54.850
She's been in bed crying.

03:56.150 --> 03:58.010
I wasn't crying.

03:59.940 --> 04:02.720
And I'm not a crybaby either.

04:02.990 --> 04:06.270
I'll do anything. Where do I start?

04:06.290 --> 04:09.980
I want you to practice your lines.
- My lines?

04:10.150 --> 04:14.300
Tomorrow you will take part in the play.
- In the play? Me?

04:15.280 --> 04:18.950
I will give you a line. Listen.

04:21.500 --> 04:28.040
I'm your new servant, General Joli-Coeur. I am at your service.

04:31.200 --> 04:32.360
Try it!

04:36.620 --> 04:37.600
Go on!

04:40.370 --> 04:46.980
I... I'm... I'm...
- I'm your new servant, General Joli-Coeur.

04:46.980 --> 04:50.120
I'm your new servant, General Joli-Coeur.

04:50.550 --> 04:56.300
I am at your service.
- Say it louder or Joli-Coeur won't hear you.

05:01.640 --> 05:06.120
Practice that for today, understood crybaby Remy?

05:13.210 --> 05:14.920
I'm not a crybaby.

05:16.090 --> 05:17.720
Definitely not.

05:24.580 --> 05:25.700
All right.

05:27.120 --> 05:31.810
I'm your new servant, General Joli-Coeur. I am at your service.

05:33.860 --> 05:39.560
I'm your new servant, General Joli-Coeur. I am at your service.

05:40.490 --> 05:44.280
Huh? I remembered it all.

05:47.680 --> 05:53.950
I'm your new servant, General Joli-Coeur. I am at your service.

06:01.280 --> 06:04.260
Yes, Joli-Coeur. Soon we'll reach the village of Ussel.

06:05.160 --> 06:06.650
The village of Ussel?

06:16.270 --> 06:19.170
Ah! Wow!

06:21.510 --> 06:23.370
This is the village of Ussel?

06:23.920 --> 06:28.160
We'll perform for lots of people here, but first we need to buy you a costume.

06:29.120 --> 06:30.480
A costume?

06:44.460 --> 06:48.930
Wow. So cute.
- That would suit you very well, Miss.

06:49.180 --> 06:52.130
Miss? Me?

07:12.230 --> 07:13.690
What do you think?

07:14.170 --> 07:18.490
Let her try it on.
- Of course. Right away.

07:28.260 --> 07:31.550
No. We need something to attract people.

07:36.810 --> 07:37.510
No.

07:45.600 --> 07:46.330
I'll take this one.

07:46.970 --> 07:50.980
Of course. Thank you very much.
- Could I borrow your scissors?

07:51.620 --> 07:53.710
My scissors?

08:08.170 --> 08:10.130
A skirt?

08:10.510 --> 08:14.390
Tomorrow you will go on stage for the first time and wear that costume.

08:15.930 --> 08:17.290
On stage?

08:28.100 --> 08:32.420
These antiques just arrived yesterday from Paris, take a look.

08:32.600 --> 08:35.620
...and I said it was impossible.

08:47.060 --> 08:50.330
I have to perform in front of all these people...

08:55.670 --> 09:00.880
I know. I've been practicing hard.
I can do it!

09:01.450 --> 09:05.720
All right, here comes the Vitalis troupe. March!

09:06.360 --> 09:09.150
Well, that's strange, isn't it?

09:17.010 --> 09:18.460
A monkey!

09:19.160 --> 09:20.790
How cute.

09:20.840 --> 09:22.400
Aren't they?

09:33.410 --> 09:34.680
Wonderful!

09:54.700 --> 09:57.950
What's wrong?
- You did that on purpose, right?

09:57.970 --> 09:59.790
I don't think she has much talent.

10:01.910 --> 10:03.280
Ladies and gentlemen!

10:03.650 --> 10:08.540
The Vitalis troupe has just come from Italy.
We will now begin our performance.

10:14.300 --> 10:16.820
Hurry and find a good spot.

10:28.470 --> 10:33.050
Amazing! Never seen anything like it.
- They're trained so well.

10:41.470 --> 10:43.880
A round of applause for our wonderful actors.

10:47.760 --> 10:50.060
Great job, everyone! Great job!

10:52.760 --> 10:55.580
And now, the main event.

10:55.930 --> 10:59.590
A special presentation by the Vitalis troupe.

11:01.620 --> 11:06.160
It's called "General Joli-Coeur and his Servant".

11:10.410 --> 11:12.430
It's my turn.

11:20.090 --> 11:23.400
General Joli-Coeur is very unhappy today.

11:25.470 --> 11:30.250
This is because his servants are lazy.

11:41.070 --> 11:44.020
I'm your new servant, General Joli-Coeur.

11:45.610 --> 11:46.380
<i>Here I go.</i>

11:46.400 --> 11:50.350
So, he decided to hire a new servant.

11:53.290 --> 11:56.980
I'm your new servant, General Joli-Coe... Ahh!

12:02.010 --> 12:06.160
What was that? That's not right.
- It must be part of the play.

12:09.180 --> 12:13.030
But as you can see, the new servant didn't improve things.

12:13.430 --> 12:15.940
Perhaps his old servants were not so bad.

12:22.930 --> 12:25.140
Those animals are smart, eh? Amazing!

12:25.160 --> 12:30.010
Hey, new girl! You should ask the dogs to teach you to do better.

12:35.740 --> 12:38.330
This concludes our performance!

12:38.540 --> 12:41.500
Please show your appreciation with a few coins.

12:57.960 --> 13:02.060
Today we earned three francs and seven cents. We did well.

13:04.000 --> 13:08.100
I practiced so hard. Why couldn't I do it?

13:12.640 --> 13:16.640
What's wrong, crybaby Remy?
- I'm not a crybaby!

13:17.900 --> 13:20.360
For the next performance, it'd be better if you sing.

13:21.470 --> 13:23.520
I think that'd be best for you.

13:25.770 --> 13:26.850
Take this.

13:28.020 --> 13:31.280
I'm going to go thank the market head.
- Okay.

13:34.430 --> 13:36.390
Guard it well.

13:37.150 --> 13:39.000
Capi, take care of everything for me.

13:46.030 --> 13:48.860
What's wrong, Sandra? You hungry?

13:52.820 --> 13:54.990
Thief!

13:57.160 --> 13:58.650
Give that back!

13:59.670 --> 14:01.710
Someone stop him!

14:04.850 --> 14:06.580
Please stop!

14:11.530 --> 14:13.330
Capi, after him!

14:13.820 --> 14:15.630
Remy? Remy, where are you?

14:15.720 --> 14:18.960
She was chasing after a thief that took your money.

14:29.100 --> 14:31.730
It's all my fault. What should I do?

14:37.720 --> 14:38.960
You found him?

14:43.490 --> 14:44.810
Find her.

15:02.560 --> 15:05.840
Mama, we have money for the doctor to come.

15:06.680 --> 15:11.840
Soon you won't be sick anymore. Don't get up.

15:12.430 --> 15:17.100
Jean, you said we have money?
Where'd you get it?

15:17.680 --> 15:21.640
Don't you worry about it, lie down.
- Jean...

15:45.820 --> 15:50.810
Jean, how'd you get the money?
- I found it lying around.

15:51.470 --> 15:55.540
I think it's a gift from father up in heaven.

15:58.740 --> 16:02.290
Jean!
- I'll see if I can get the doctor.

16:08.330 --> 16:12.050
I'm sorry. I'm...

16:12.270 --> 16:18.440
Well... It's a gift from your father in heaven, right?

16:24.380 --> 16:27.630
I won't let it happen again.

16:33.060 --> 16:35.960
Take good care of your mother.

16:38.460 --> 16:41.800
Thank you. Thank you so much.

16:42.980 --> 16:46.510
What should I do?
I can't ask him to return it.

16:47.940 --> 16:51.390
But the money was very important to Mr. Vitalis.

16:52.430 --> 16:55.520
<i>For the next performance, it'd be better if you sing.</i>

16:56.730 --> 16:57.670
Sing?

16:58.120 --> 17:00.360
<i>I think that'd be best for you.</i>

17:00.900 --> 17:02.680
That's it. I'll try that.

17:03.390 --> 17:06.760
Huh? Really?
- Would you like to hear a song?

17:07.110 --> 17:08.300
A song?
- Yes.

17:08.300 --> 17:10.240
Is the dog going to sing?

17:11.550 --> 17:15.670
No, I'm going to.
- Then I'm not interested.

17:15.880 --> 17:18.360
So as I was saying...
- What happened?

17:19.170 --> 17:21.620
Um, would you like to...
- Get out of the way!

17:22.610 --> 17:24.230
Would you like to hear a song?

17:26.670 --> 17:29.990
Please, listen to my song.

17:30.540 --> 17:35.330
Listen to my song and if you like it, please give me some coins.

17:35.330 --> 17:37.930
Nobody's interested in a tramp's song.

17:51.200 --> 17:52.850
I wonder why nobody wants to hear my song.

18:02.110 --> 18:03.400
Sis!

18:05.260 --> 18:06.270
Nana!

18:07.950 --> 18:10.670
What are you doing here?
- I'm not Nana.

18:11.430 --> 18:15.550
I'm Catherine.
- I'm sorry. But...

18:18.150 --> 18:23.520
You look a lot like my sister.
- Sorry if my daughter has bothered you.

18:23.930 --> 18:28.850
I saw you at the market and Catherine would love to hear you sing.

18:29.530 --> 18:33.100
But since we're not rich, we can't give you much money.

18:33.500 --> 18:34.660
Will you sing for her?

18:36.120 --> 18:37.840
Please sing, Sis!

18:44.360 --> 18:54.780
Mother, mother, my mother

18:55.070 --> 19:03.490
Your gentle hugs holding me

19:03.650 --> 19:11.130
When I'm lonely and sleeping at night

19:12.730 --> 19:17.920
Her heart is my hometown

19:18.640 --> 19:23.950
My mother

19:27.320 --> 19:37.790
Mother, mother, my mother

19:38.010 --> 19:44.350
I'll wander the land forever

19:44.490 --> 19:54.710
My heart is singing

19:55.600 --> 20:01.180
Her heart is my hometown

20:01.640 --> 20:08.770
My mother...

20:23.750 --> 20:26.830
Wonderful! What a wonderful song.

20:26.900 --> 20:28.440
Let's go, Catherine.
- Okay.

20:29.410 --> 20:32.210
Here, thank you so much, Sis!

20:32.680 --> 20:39.740
Sorry we can't give you more.
- It is I who should be thanking you.

20:42.900 --> 20:46.360
Well, Catherine, let's go home. Mother is waiting.

20:46.580 --> 20:48.960
Okay. Goodbye, Sis!

20:49.520 --> 20:51.230
Goodbye, Catherine.

21:07.830 --> 21:12.830
I'm very sorry. I lost all the money except for this.

21:19.090 --> 21:25.170
Keep this money since it's the first that you earned. It's very important.

21:27.540 --> 21:30.310
Well, let's go!
- Mr. Vitalis!

21:31.920 --> 21:33.330
Thank you.

21:40.170 --> 21:42.100
Let's go, crybaby Remy.

21:42.550 --> 21:50.850
Try to love youself more

21:52.150 --> 22:01.650
Abandoned dreams can be seen again

22:01.750 --> 22:10.450
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:11.150 --> 22:22.650
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:22.850 --> 22:32.750
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:32.950 --> 22:42.550
From the future that gives us our fate

22:42.750 --> 22:50.850
Try to seek for them more

22:52.250 --> 22:56.150
Give your heart to

22:56.250 --> 23:10.950
That person who is also seeking you

23:19.740 --> 23:21.710
Again... another letter.

23:23.450 --> 23:27.740
Why? Why did he sell such an important thing?

23:29.130 --> 23:32.350
Remy, this magic story hasn't finished yet.

23:32.600 --> 23:36.770
<i>A Great Gift</i>

23:32.600 --> 23:36.770
Next time:
